WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.136
-Let's go back
to earlier this year.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.004
Do you remember that?
The Grammy --

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.405
At the Grammy Awards,

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.475
you guys took home 11 Grammys
between both of you

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.577
for "When We All Fall Asleep."

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:13.646
What do --
That's what I call it.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.116
I abbreviate it now.
-[ Laughs ] It's okay.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.752
-I say "When We" now.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.487
When you guys recorded
"When We"...

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.823
-[ Laughs ] "When We."

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:27.927
-No, but what do you remember
about that night?

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.362
-It was amazing.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:33.166
It was, like, one of
the best nights ever for me.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:38.538
I -- Uh, yeah,
it was pretty peak, I would say.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.973
-[ Laughs ]
-You know?

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.574
-Yeah. Yeah. I would say so.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.643
-But it was also, like,
not because we won.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.511
It was just because...
-We were there.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.281
-...that we were there. Like,
you know, just being there --

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:52.718
Just being nominated
is so amazing and rare,

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.653
so, you know,
that was -- that was --

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:56.489
We were already happy.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.391
I remember when we got there
that morning,

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.227
me and Finneas were like,
"We're good.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.196
We don't need to win.
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.498
-We don't need --
Like, we're already here.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.633
You know, we're not worried.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.235
If we win or if we don't win,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.137
it's just amazing
that we get to be here."

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.106
And, crazily...
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.340
-Yeah.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.209
You wouldn't even guess it.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.012
Crazily, you kept winning.
Yeah.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.446
-Yep.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.282
-I loved --
They cut to you, Billie,

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.749
right before I think it was

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.752
Album of the Year,
Record of the Year.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.986
And they cut to you,
and you were mouthing,

00:01:27.986 --> 00:01:29.455
"Please don't be me."

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.890
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.526
-I was like, "That is so you."
Like, "Please don't be me."

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.061
And I think I know
why you were doing it.

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:38.364
'Cause I -- Not like
we're best friends or anything,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.468
but I feel like, knowing you,
you're going like, "I'm good.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:46.138
I had a good night. I'm good.
Let's end this now."

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:50.043
Is that what you were thinking,
or what were you...?

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.278
-You know,
I don't know what I --

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:57.350
I was very overwhelmed,
but only in a way of...

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.984
it's so amazing,
I can't believe it.

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.120
Not like, "I don't want..."
You know what I mean?

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.688
-Yeah. No. Yeah.
-It's like --

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.959
how can you feel like
you deserve that kind of thing?

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.661
But I will say, though,
that the next day,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.530
we were over here,
and Alicia Keys called me,

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.100
and she wanted
to congratulate me.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.036
And she basically
said on the phone,

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.973
which is something that I, like,
hold so dear to me, which is --

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.974
'Cause, you know,
she won a billion Grammys

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.744
when she was really young --
her first Grammys I think.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.813
And she called me,
and she was like,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:32.018
"I just wanted to say don't be
embarrassed for being dope."

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.519
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.387
That is so her, by the way.

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:37.890
-So good.
-That is so her.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.826
-It's true. Yeah.
-Are you guys --

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:45.365
You were on tour
or like three dates into it,

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.233
and then you had to cancel?

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.001
-Yep.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.003
-Bummer?
Or were you a little bit like,

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.272
"Oh, yeah, maybe
I needed a little break"?

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:54.774
Or I don't know.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.242
-Kind of both.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.512
I was really looking forward
to that tour for like months.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:04.217
Um, but, you know...
[Laughs] at the time,

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.020
we were like, "Well,
we could use two weeks off."

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.322
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
Cut to six months off.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.723
You're like, "Okay."
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:13.158
So, yeah, it was great

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:15.595
for like the first couple weeks,
first month,

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.831
and then it was like, "Okay.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.367
You know.
When can this be done?"

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.369
But we have made the best of it,
I would say.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:27.106
I think we've really done what
we should've done in this time,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.876
and we've made a lot of music,

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.145
and I don't think
we would have made it otherwise

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:34.880
if we hadn't have gotten
this time.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.583
So as much as it's been terrible
to have, you know,

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.652
this going on in the world,
I think it has...

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.854
-We've been really lucky.
-...birthed some things.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.656
We have been really lucky
with it, I think.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.059
-And you're happy
with the songs you wrote?

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.693
-Yeah, we're writing a lot.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.929
-Yeah, I love them.
-It's really fun.

